  "end": {
    "line": "A new jewelry story every day",
    "handle": "HeyGema"
  },
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "This green gem turns red by candlelight.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "hook",
        "show": "gem",
        "shape": "oval",
        "tone": "#2f9a78",
        "toneTo": "#c0305a",
        "color": "#f7c23a"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Miners found it in Russia's emerald mines in the early 1830s.",
      "say": "Miners found it in Russia's emerald mines in the early eighteen thirties.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "mine",
        "place": "Ural Mountains, Russia",
        "year": "1830s",
        "tone": "#2f9a78",
        "color": "#5bb4e8"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "A Finnish mineralogist, Nils Nordenskiöld, first took one for an emerald.",
      "say": "A Finnish mineralogist, Nils Noor-den-shold, first took one for an emerald.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "cast",
        "setting": "study",
        "name": "Nils Gustaf Nordenskiöld",
        "role": "Finnish mineralogist",
        "color": "#ec6a9c",
        "cast": [
          {
            "outfit": "coat",
            "outfitColor": "#3a4a6a",
            "hair": "side",
            "hairColor": "#8a6a4a",
            "facial": "mustache",
            "skin": "#f1cfb0",
            "expression": "focused",
            "prop": "gem",
            "propTone": "#2f9a78"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Its hardness puzzled him,",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "cast",
        "setting": "study",
        "color": "#c8dc3c",
        "cast": [
          {
            "outfit": "coat",
            "outfitColor": "#3a4a6a",
            "hair": "side",
            "hairColor": "#8a6a4a",
            "facial": "mustache",
            "skin": "#f1cfb0",
            "expression": "worried",
            "glasses": "loupe",
            "prop": "magnifier"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "and that evening, by candlelight, the stone turned red.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "reveal",
        "item": "gem",
        "shape": "oval",
        "tone": "#c0305a",
        "light": "#ffb347",
        "dark": true,
        "label": "By candlelight",
        "color": "#a98be0"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "It was a new kind of chrysoberyl, colored by a little chromium.",
      "say": "It was a new kind of kriss-oh-berrill, colored by a little chromium.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "Chromium",
        "sub": "In a new chrysoberyl",
        "color": "#4cc3a8"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "It soaks up yellow light, so the lamp decides its color.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "reveal",
        "item": "gem",
        "shape": "oval",
        "tone": "#2f9a78",
        "toneTo": "#c0305a",
        "label": "Daylight and lamplight",
        "color": "#f7c23a"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "It was named for the future Tsar Alexander II.",
      "say": "It was named for the future Tsar Alexander the Second.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "portrait",
        "name": "Alexander II",
        "years": "The future Tsar",
        "hair": "side",
        "hairColor": "#6b4a2e",
        "dress": "#2f4f8a",
        "color": "#f0552e"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Legend says it was given to him on his sixteenth birthday.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "gift",
        "stone": "oval",
        "tone": "#2f9a78",
        "to": "For Alexander",
        "date": "Legend, 1834",
        "color": "#5bb4e8"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Its red and green were imperial Russia's military colors.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "Red and\ngreen",
        "sub": "Imperial Russia's colors",
        "color": "#c8dc3c"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Since 1952, it's been a birthstone for June.",
      "say": "Since nineteen fifty-two, it's been a birthstone for June.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "jewel",
        "piece": "ring",
        "shape": "oval",
        "tone": "#2f9a78",
        "metal": "yellow",
        "label": "June birthstone",
        "color": "#ec6a9c"
      }
    }
  ],
  "post": {
    "caption": "Green in daylight, red by candlelight. The gem a mineralogist first took for an emerald.",
